WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.450
During coexistence, Entra ID
learns to check the card itself.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.472
You load the PIV issuers
into its trust store,

3
00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:10.657
give it a revocation list
it can reach over HTTP,

4
00:00:10.657 --> 00:00:15.475
and users can sign in to Windows with
their card on Entra-joined devices.

5
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:19.670
The binding between card and person
lives in certificate user IDs,

6
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.950
and for synced users only
Entra Connect can write it.

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.734
There's one tension worth naming: the
federal guide suggests a looser binding,

8
00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:30.575
while Microsoft says use
only the strict kind.

9
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:35.300
The program uses the strict kind,
tied to one specific certificate.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.390
So what happens when sync goes away?
